-- title:
--   Regular parameter pair (varpi,t) when A/varpi A is a DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $A$ be a commutative ring which is an integral domain and local, with maximal ideal $\mathfrak m_A =$ `IsLocalRing.maximalIdeal A`, and let $\varpi \in A$ be an element of $\mathfrak m_A$ with $\varpi \neq 0$ such that the quotient $A/(\varpi)$, by the ideal generated by the singleton $\{\varpi\}$, is an integral domain and a discrete valuation ring. Then there exists $t \in A$ such that, first, the ideal generated by the entries of the list $[\varpi, t]$ equals $\mathfrak m_A$, i.e. $\mathfrak m_A = (\varpi, t)$; and second, $[\varpi, t]$ is a regular sequence on $A$ viewed as a module over itself in the sense of `RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular`: multiplication by $\varpi$ is injective on $A$, multiplication by $t$ is injective on $A/\varpi A$, and the final quotient $A/(\varpi, t)$ is nonzero. Note that the discrete valuation ring hypothesis on $A/(\varpi)$ is an instance assumption, as is the assumption that this quotient is a domain.
--
--   This is the standard statement that a nonzero $\varpi \in \mathfrak m_A$ whose quotient ring is a discrete valuation ring extends to a regular system of parameters of the two-dimensional regular local ring $A$. It is used at a closed point of the smooth locus of the special fibre of a semistable model, where $A$ is the local ring of the model and $A/\varpi A$ the local ring of the smooth special fibre, supplying the regular sequence and the generation of the maximal ideal required by the miracle-flatness criterion behind [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.flat_pi`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.flat_pi).
